{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All code changes will be compatible with Spring Framework 6.0+ and Java 17+ as specified in the framework requirements.",
    "The pluggable runtime SPI for module deployment (U7) will use Java's ServiceLoader mechanism for pluggability, consistent with standard Spring extension patterns.",
    "The Boot-based ModuleRunner (U8) will leverage Spring Boot's embedded servlet container support to eliminate the hard dependency on xd-containers.",
    "Performance benchmarks for U4 and U5 will use the Java Microbenchmark Harness (JMH) to ensure accurate, reproducible performance measurements.",
    "The CI build install target (U2) will be implemented using Maven, the standard build tool for Spring ecosystem projects.",
    "GPDB parameter UX simplification (U6) will use Spring's data binding and validation utilities to eliminate manual parameter escaping requirements."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Access to all existing relevant code repositories (Spring XD, DEBS challenge, Sqoop, GPDB, Kafka integrations) with up-to-date code and documentation is available.",
    "The in-use CI system (e.g., GitHub Actions, Jenkins) is compatible with Maven build configurations and supports custom target execution.",
    "Test environments for SQLServer, GPDB, and performance benchmarking are pre-provisioned with required access credentials, consistent hardware specs, and match the environment of prior benchmark runs for valid comparison.",
    "The existing repository abstraction code for stream/job definitions is well-documented to support migration to a pluggable runtime SPI (U7).",
    "Remaining DEBS challenge work (U1) is limited to pre-defined pending tasks with no new scope additions, aligned with the challenge submission deadline.",
    "The samples repository has established contribution guidelines that the XD + Kafka POC will adhere to for acceptance."
  ],
